votal political institution in South Asia, having been established on June 23, 1949, in Dhaka, Bangladesh. As one of the two dominant political parties in the country, alongside the Bangladesh Nationalist Party, the Awami League played a crucial role in shaping the modern political landscape of Bangladesh. Its founding figures, including Sheikh Mujibur Rahman, who later became the nation's first president, sought to address the socio-political grievances of East Pakistan (now Bangladesh) during a time of significant political and economic disparity with West Pakistan.

